  "question": {
    "text": "Let $S=\\mathbf{N} \\cup\\{0\\}$. Define a relation $R$ from $S$ to $\\mathbf{R}$ by :\n$\\mathrm{R}=\\left\\{(x, y): \\log _{\\mathrm{e}} y=x \\log _{\\mathrm{e}}\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right), x \\in \\mathrm{~S}, y \\in \\mathbf{R}\\right\\}$\n\nThen, the sum of all the elements in the range of $R$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{10}{9}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & S=\\{0,1,2,3 \\ldots \\ldots\\} \\\\ & \\log _y y=\\log _e\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow y=\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^x\\end{aligned}$\n\n\n\n<img src=\"assets\\st0016_6d892db0283d.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n\nRequired\n$\\text { Sum }=1+\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^1+\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^3+\\ldots . .-=\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{2}{5}}=\\frac{5}{3}$"
  }
}